# =====================================================================
# Release V157 -- PBI.[List Patients] gains Effectively_Active
# =====================================================================
# The Day Book detail drill-through pages filter ONLY on the fact condition -- Is Cancelled /
# Is DNA / Course Status / recall scope -- with no patient predicate at all. So they list far more
# than the tile counts: on tenant 100, 2,185 cancellation rows behind a tile reading 1,157, and
# 453 DNA rows behind 261. That mismatch pre-dates V155/V156; those releases widened it.
#
# Power BI cannot express "attended within two years" from the base views, so Gold.vw_Dim_Patients
# supplies the flag. It reads Gold.vw_Effectively_Active_Patients rather than restating the rule,
# so there is still exactly one definition.
#
# Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views prefers a vw_<table> override over the table, so this becomes
# PBI.[List Patients] automatically -- the same mechanism vw_Dim_Practitioners uses. Purely
# ADDITIVE: all 51 existing columns pass through unchanged and in order, so no existing report
# binding can break.
#
# AFTER DEPLOY, in this order:
#   1. Refresh the shared semantic model in Power BI Desktop so [List Patients] picks up the new
#      column. Nothing changes in any report until this is done.
#   2. THEN open Day_Book.pbip and publish -- the four detail pages filter on the new column, and
#      opening before step 1 will show them as referencing a missing field.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V157__list_patients_effectively_active.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.vw_Dim_Patients.View.sql
EXEC     EXEC Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views;

TEST
